&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The work you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot;&gt;Evaluate &amp;amp; Prototype RAG Solutions: Assist in designing, prototyping, and testing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) frameworks to make Celonis&#39;s organizational knowledge base AI-ready and queryable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot;&gt;Data Prep &amp;amp; Optimization: Partner with Data teams to evaluate data chunking strategies, metadata tagging, and vector database management to optimize the retrieval performance of internal KM tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot;&gt;Bridge the Gap Between KM and Tech: Act as a key technical liaison with the Data, Analysis, and Technology teams to translate KM workflow needs into scalable data pipelines and architectural requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot;&gt;Collaborative Technical Alignment: Participate in cross-functional technical syncs to ensure KM&#39;s architectural roadmap aligns perfectly with the broader enterprise technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,4,0&quot;&gt;Engage Stakeholders: Propose innovative approaches to knowledge-sharing challenges, facilitate problem-solving sessions, and encourage participation in knowledge management initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The qualifications you need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot;&gt;Academic Background: Graduates from a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a highly quantitative technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot;&gt;Foundational CS &amp;amp; RAG Concepts: Solid understanding of data structures, algorithms, and fundamental NLP/LLM concepts—specifically how embedding models, vector search, and retrieval mechanisms work under the hood.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot;&gt;Technical Tools &amp;amp; Experimentation: Proficient in Python with a solid grasp of agentic architectures. Experience building academic or personal projects involving LLM APIs (like OpenAI, Anthropic, or open-source models via Hugging Face) and vector stores (e.g., Pinecone, Chroma, FAISS) is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Communication: Excellent interpersonal and communication skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,4,0&quot;&gt;Systemic Problem Solving: Passionate about building automated pipelines and intelligent agents to handle data sanitization, eliminating the need for manual, error-prone human tagging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,5,0&quot;&gt;Reliability &amp;amp; Drive: Strong time management skills, comfort with public speaking, and the ability to connect complex ideas and solve problems independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,6,0&quot;&gt;Experience: Prior internship experience in relevant technical or data domains is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9,7,0&quot;&gt;Language: Excellent verbal and written communication in English.&lt;/li&gt;
