&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Monks, we believe in fostering an environment where a diversity of perspectives can thrive. We proactively work to design hiring processes that promote equity and inclusion while mitigating bias. We celebrate diversity and are committed to building a team that reflects the communities we serve. We welcome and encourage qualified applicants, from all backgrounds, who are excited to contribute to our mission.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-FP1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Monks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks is the global, digital-first, data-driven, unitary operating brand of S4 Capital plc. With a legacy of innovation and specialized expertise, Monks combines an extraordinary range of global Marketing and Technology Services to redefine how brands interact with the world. Through Monks.Flow, its flagship AI ecosystem for marketing orchestration, Monks transforms marketing into a growth engine, collapsing timelines and connecting brands to culture in real time. By deploying bespoke intelligent agents across disciplines and delivering culturally relevant, high-impact creative and digital solutions, Monks solves key critical business challenges across the entire brand enterprise to help brands sustain long-term impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services, ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-25) and remains the only partner featured in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). Named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023) and The One Show’s inaugural AI Pioneer Organization, Monks was also awarded Business Intelligence Group’s 2025 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Award in both the Organizational and AI Product categories. As a trusted partner to cutting-edge innovators in tech, Monks earned titles such as Optimizely Experimentation Partner of the Year (2025), runner-up for the Adobe Firefly Partner Award (2024), and Workato’s AI Visionary Customer Impact Award (2024). Additionally, Monks achieved a record-breaking number of FWAs and continues to hold the most of any partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a respectful and empowering work environment for all people to freely express themselves amongst colleagues who embrace diversity in all respects. Including fresh voices and unique points of view in all aspects of our business not only creates an environment where we can all grow and thrive but also increases our potential to produce work that better represents—and resonates with—the world around us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;monks.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strong Account Director to lead a high-profile CPG program. This role requires a strong operator, strategic partner, and team leader who can navigate fast-moving businesses, complex stakeholder ecosystems, and high-volume creative production while driving exceptional work and client trust. This person will help sustain structure and clarity to campaigns across a portfolio of 13+ brands by building scalable processes, managing cross-functional coordination, and keeping teams aligned from planning through execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role involves sustaining success on the program, problem solving operational/management challenges that arise, managing the delivery of key projects, collaborating with program leads at the client organization, and working closely with the internal leadership team across our agency collective. The ideal candidate is proactive, organized, and comfortable navigating ambiguity. They know how to keep momentum moving, ask thoughtful questions, and partner effectively across creative, operations, and stakeholder teams in an environment with evolving priorities and frequent reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible role requiring both executive presence and hands-on leadership within a collaborative integrated agency environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Relationship &amp;amp; Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic client relationships (day to day &amp;amp; senior levels), positioning the team as a true business partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate complex feedback loops and stakeholder management with confidence and diplomacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment across clients, internal teams, and partner agencies within the integrated agency team (IAT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build key relationships with internal discipline leads as well as lead, mentor, and support account team members across levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative, solutions-oriented team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage strategic thinking, accountability, and strong client stewardship across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead full Program team to sustain success and further drive efficiency and quality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with creative, strategy, and production teams to deliver integrated solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage high-volume workflows across multiple concurrent projects and asset builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive efficiencies across timelines, briefing processes, feedback management, and resource allocation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor account health including scopes, utilization, burn management, SLAs, and delivery KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational risks early and proactively develop solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with project management to ensure teams are set up for success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to financial forecasting and internal revenue management activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with an internal cross-functional team to ensure deliverables are produced on time, on budget, and to client’s specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creative Development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead creative process from briefing to execution across multiple client deliverables, including digital advertising/marketing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with clients on creative briefs to communicate project requirements for strategy, creative, and copywriting teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and update all project timelines, manage spreadsheets, creative folders and other shared documents across platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage all processes required to obtain a range of client approvals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain excellent written and verbal communication with all parties.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for leading ad campaign delivery for Procter &amp;amp; Gamble, focusing primarily on digital execution, and occasionally on TV and print. Provide general leadership for the account team, with two direct reports, while maintaining overall oversight of the team’s operational health. Scope ranges from tactical campaigns—including minor adaptations and resizing—to high-complexity projects involving strategy, creative development, and full-scale production shoots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
