&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-12+ years of marketing experience in a fast-paced, independent environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to execute large-scale strategies and programs, with experience managing diverse set of digital marketing programs mapping back to larger strategy and objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write a campaign brief and give strong direction to the creative team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong confident communicator with executive presence and relationship building skills with key partners and stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills to organize teams across complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are looking for someone with a strong production/PM background for creative assets rather than a purely commercial AD. Understanding the &#39;soft side&#39;—the back-and-forth of creative ideas—is definitely a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A plus - experience managing large enterprise or Fortune 500 accounts, preferably within CPG or healthcare categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in AI-enabled marketing workflows, innovation, and operational transformation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
