&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services, ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-25) and remains the only partner featured in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). Named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023) and The One Show’s inaugural AI Pioneer Organization, Monks was also awarded Business Intelligence Group’s 2025 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Award in both the Organizational and AI Product categories. As a trusted partner to cutting-edge innovators in tech, Monks earned titles such as Optimizely Experimentation Partner of the Year (2025), runner-up for the Adobe Firefly Partner Award (2024), and Workato’s AI Visionary Customer Impact Award (2024). Additionally, Monks achieved a record-breaking number of FWAs and continues to hold the most of any partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a respectful and empowering work environment for all people to freely express themselves amongst colleagues who embrace diversity in all respects. Including fresh voices and unique points of view in all aspects of our business not only creates an environment where we can all grow and thrive but also increases our potential to produce work that better represents—and resonates with—the world around us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;monks.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a BI Analyst to build and maintain media reporting solutions for both internal stakeholders and external clients. This is a hybrid client-facing and internal delivery role: you will develop dashboards, extract insights to inform campaign decisions, and tailor reporting outputs to client needs across engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;​​Key responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build and maintain robust dashboards, reports and visualizations that track media campaign performance and KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze complex data sets in-depth to identify trends, callout issues, and gather insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights and analytical support to cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with clients and internal teams to understand their measurement needs, configure reports, and present findings that support data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate and maintain multiple data sources (ad platforms, analytics, attribution, CRM) using connectors and ETL/data integration tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document data flows, transformations and report definitions to ensure transparency and reproducibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively detect and troubleshoot data quality issues; collaborate with stakeholders to identify solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvements in reporting processes, templates and automation to scale delivery and reduce manual effort.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience you already have&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with BI/visualization tools such as Google Looker Studio, Tableau, Power BI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with strong time and project management skills, and high attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills including the ability to analyze and resolve complex problems using data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize complex data into concise insights and actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced English. This will be tested during the selection process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge on Media, including media reporting tools (DV360, SA360, Meta, etc.) and web analytics tools (Google Analytics, Adobe Analytics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with data connectors (e.g., Supermetrics, Tracer, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or coursework with a cloud platform (GCP, AWS, Azure) or BigQuery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in an agency or client-side media analytics roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;About us&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks is a digital-first marketing and advertising services company connecting content, data &amp;amp; digital media, and technology services. Our single-P&amp;amp;L model gives brands seamless access to a nearly 6,000-strong team of digital talent across 57 talent hubs in 33 countries. We value diverse perspectives and foster an inclusive environment where everyone can bring their authentic self. Join us to help shape the future of the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Media Analytics team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Monks expands our Global Enterprise Analytics capabilities, the Media Analytics team delivers media performance reporting, measurement, and data-driven insights that enable clients to optimize campaigns and make smarter media decisions. Our analysts partner with media, strategy, data engineering, and client teams to design scalable reporting solutions and translate complex data into clear, actionable recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
