&lt;li&gt;Help clients build their data maturity roadmap and advocate for initiatives that deliver both short-term wins and long-term capability uplift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide informed recommendations on platform choices, architecture decisions, and analytics strategy in close partnership with technical specialists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; SOW Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and manage Statements of Work (SOWs), ensuring scope, assumptions, and commercial terms are clearly defined and mutually agreed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee billing, budget tracking, and financial reconciliation across your accounts - flag overruns early and manage change control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate account records in Salesforce and internal project management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in client-facing roles - account management, digital consulting, or client services, ideally in data, analytics, or digital marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural relationship builder with a track record of growing accounts and managing senior stakeholder relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with budgets, SOWs, renewal conversations, and identifying upsell opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with analytics platforms (GA4, Adobe Analytics) and digital marketing ecosystems (DV360, CM360, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator who can translate technical concepts into business language — written, verbal, and in presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-paced, cross-functional environment. Confident working with both onshore and offshore teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise procurement processes and complex billing structures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to cloud environments (GCP, AWS) or data engineering / analytics engineering concepts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MarTech or data platforms (Adobe Experience Platform, Salesforce Marketing Cloud, Braze, or similar) highly desirable&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Google Analytics, Adobe Analytics, or Google Cloud certification highly preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-CX1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Monks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks is the global, digital-first, data-driven, unitary operating brand of S4 Capital plc. With a legacy of innovation and specialized expertise, Monks combines an extraordinary range of global Marketing and Technology Services to redefine how brands interact with the world. Through Monks.Flow, its flagship AI ecosystem for marketing orchestration, Monks transforms marketing into a growth engine, collapsing timelines and connecting brands to culture in real time. By deploying bespoke intelligent agents across disciplines and delivering culturally relevant, high-impact creative and digital solutions, Monks solves key critical business challenges across the entire brand enterprise to help brands sustain long-term impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services, ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-25) and remains the only partner featured in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). Named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023) and The One Show’s inaugural AI Pioneer Organization, Monks was also awarded Business Intelligence Group’s 2025 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Award in both the Organizational and AI Product categories. As a trusted partner to cutting-edge innovators in tech, Monks earned titles such as Optimizely Experimentation Partner of the Year (2025), runner-up for the Adobe Firefly Partner Award (2024), and Workato’s AI Visionary Customer Impact Award (2024). Additionally, Monks achieved a record-breaking number of FWAs and continues to hold the most of any partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a respectful and empowering work environment for all people to freely express themselves amongst colleagues who embrace diversity in all respects. Including fresh voices and unique points of view in all aspects of our business not only creates an environment where we can all grow and thrive but also increases our potential to produce work that better represents—and resonates with—the world around us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;monks.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, delivery-first role for an experienced engagement professional who thrives in complex, multi-workstream environments. As a Data Engagement Manager you will be the operational backbone of our Australian client engagements - running the end-to-end delivery engine while working in close partnership with onshore Engagement Managers and the Director of Client Partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not just execute - you will elevate. You bring strong project management rigour, a continuous improvement mindset, and enough client-facing capability to contribute meaningfully to stakeholder conversations when needed. You thrive on building systems, identifying delivery gaps, and setting the standard for how work gets done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1. Delivery Leadership &amp;amp; Project Governance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end accountability for the delivery of complex, multi-workstream data and analytics engagements across the Australian client portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the project management lifecycle — scoping, planning, resourcing, execution, quality assurance, and closure — across multiple concurrent accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce delivery standards, change control procedures, and escalation frameworks across all active engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain real-time visibility of delivery health across your accounts — proactively flag risks, resolve blockers, and manage competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead sprint planning, stand-ups, and delivery reviews with offshore squads — keep momentum high and accountability clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2. Continuous Improvement &amp;amp; Process Development&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps, inefficiencies, and recurring delivery issues — then build systems, templates, and playbooks to fix them at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish repeatable delivery frameworks that can be adopted across the wider team — onboarding, QA checklists, handover protocols, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run retrospectives and lessons learned sessions after key delivery milestones, turning insight into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a culture of quality and continuous improvement within the delivery team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Director of Client Partnerships to shape the delivery operating model as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3. Client Engagement &amp;amp; Stakeholder Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with onshore Engagement Managers to ensure delivery context is clearly communicated to clients at all times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in client-facing delivery reviews, QBRs, and milestone presentations where appropriate — contribute to the narrative around delivery progress and next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear and proactive communication with onshore counterparts — no surprises, ever.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support SOW scoping by providing accurate effort estimates, resource plans, and delivery assumptions based on hands-on experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4. Commercial &amp;amp; SOW Accountability&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate within agreed SOW scope and budget — track actuals vs. estimates and flag variances early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce scope governance rigorously — identify out-of-scope requests, assess impact, and feed back into the commercial conversation with the Engagement Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to accurate and timely invoicing by providing delivery milestones, hours logged, and completion sign-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in technical project delivery, engagement management, or digital consulting — preferably in data, analytics, or MarTech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to run complex, multi-workstream projects with strict governance, change control, and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of identifying delivery problems and building systems to solve them — not just fixing the symptom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing offshore or cross-functional teams. Comfortable holding people accountable with empathy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data and analytics platforms (GA4, Adobe Analytics, GCP, BigQuery, etc.). Able to QA technical outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, structured communicator — able to synthesise delivery complexity into concise updates for onshore EMs and client stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP, PRINCE2, or equivalent project management certification.&amp;nbsp;Exposure to Agile delivery frameworks (Scrum, Kanban) and experience running hybrid delivery models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling delivery processes in a consulting or professional services context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with platform ecosystem: Google Marketing Platform, Adobe Experience Platform, Salesforce Marketing Cloud, or similar highly desirable&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Australian enterprise clients or in a global delivery model would be a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-CX1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Monks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks is the global, digital-first, data-driven, unitary operating brand of S4 Capital plc. With a legacy of innovation and specialized expertise, Monks combines an extraordinary range of global Marketing and Technology Services to redefine how brands interact with the world. Through Monks.Flow, its flagship AI ecosystem for marketing orchestration, Monks transforms marketing into a growth engine, collapsing timelines and connecting brands to culture in real time. By deploying bespoke intelligent agents across disciplines and delivering culturally relevant, high-impact creative and digital solutions, Monks solves key critical business challenges across the entire brand enterprise to help brands sustain long-term impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services, ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-25) and remains the only partner featured in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). Named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023) and The One Show’s inaugural AI Pioneer Organization, Monks was also awarded Business Intelligence Group’s 2025 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Award in both the Organizational and AI Product categories. As a trusted partner to cutting-edge innovators in tech, Monks earned titles such as Optimizely Experimentation Partner of the Year (2025), runner-up for the Adobe Firefly Partner Award (2024), and Workato’s AI Visionary Customer Impact Award (2024). Additionally, Monks achieved a record-breaking number of FWAs and continues to hold the most of any partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a respectful and empowering work environment for all people to freely express themselves amongst colleagues who embrace diversity in all respects. Including fresh voices and unique points of view in all aspects of our business not only creates an environment where we can all grow and thrive but also increases our potential to produce work that better represents—and resonates with—the world around us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;monks.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Data Engineer at Monks, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to grow and contribute to exciting projects by helping to design, build, and maintain data pipelines and cloud infrastructure. The data engineer should have a strong foundational understanding of cloud environment, data pipelines, data cleansing, and basic data warehousing. Ideally, you possess a foundational understanding of machine learning concepts, allowing you to bridge the gap between engineering and advanced marketing analytics applications. This role is an excellent opportunity for those looking to build a career in data engineering and data science.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Netherlands-based role requires supporting the Data Strategy team with a major Netherlands client. We offer a dynamic and challenging work environment at the forefront of AI-driven innovation in marketing. If you&#39;re passionate about pushing the boundaries of what’s possible, we encourage you to apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop data pipelines and solutions across cloud platforms such as AWS and GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the authentication and integration of platform APIs and help automate an end to end ETL processes for data integration and transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate and collaborate in the design and implementation of data models and data warehouses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop data transformation recipes that efficiently transform raw data into structured formats suitable for data warehousing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and maintain with the documentation for data models, including architecture diagrams, schema, definitions, and metadata.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and troubleshoot data pipelines’ issues to ensure timely data availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the data science team to integrate and build ML models and Gen-AI applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess good data literacy and understand how technical data applications create business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate progress and findings to both technical and non-technical team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to work independently and in a team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor or Masters in a quantitative subject such as Data Science, Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of working experience in data science or data engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate Cloud Certification such as GCP Cloud Architect, Data Engineer, Machine Learning Engineer or any equivalent.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and SQL.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in authenticating and authorising API requests using methods such as OAuth and API keys and troubleshooting common API-related challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of data structures and databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of data modeling concepts and tools such as dbt or Dataform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of data warehousing and ETL concepts and experience with tools like Amazon Redshift or Google BigQuery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data privacy principles and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English communication and written skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor or Masters Degree in Data Science.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Cloud Certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD and version control tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with marketing analytics tools and data (e.g. Google Analytics, Adobe Analytics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with social data&amp;nbsp; (e.g. Instragram, Facebook, Tiktok).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with machine learning and Gen-AI models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Monks, we believe in fostering an environment where a diversity of perspectives can thrive. We proactively work to design hiring processes that promote equity and inclusion while mitigating bias. We celebrate diversity and are committed to building a team that reflects the communities we serve. We welcome and encourage qualified applicants, from all backgrounds, who are excited to contribute to our mission.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-FP1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Monks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks is the global, digital-first, data-driven, unitary operating brand of S4 Capital plc. With a legacy of innovation and specialized expertise, Monks combines an extraordinary range of global Marketing and Technology Services to redefine how brands interact with the world. Through Monks.Flow, its flagship AI ecosystem for marketing orchestration, Monks transforms marketing into a growth engine, collapsing timelines and connecting brands to culture in real time. By deploying bespoke intelligent agents across disciplines and delivering culturally relevant, high-impact creative and digital solutions, Monks solves key critical business challenges across the entire brand enterprise to help brands sustain long-term impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services, ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-25) and remains the only partner featured in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). Named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023) and The One Show’s inaugural AI Pioneer Organization, Monks was also awarded Business Intelligence Group’s 2025 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Award in both the Organizational and AI Product categories. As a trusted partner to cutting-edge innovators in tech, Monks earned titles such as Optimizely Experimentation Partner of the Year (2025), runner-up for the Adobe Firefly Partner Award (2024), and Workato’s AI Visionary Customer Impact Award (2024). Additionally, Monks achieved a record-breaking number of FWAs and continues to hold the most of any partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a respectful and empowering work environment for all people to freely express themselves amongst colleagues who embrace diversity in all respects. Including fresh voices and unique points of view in all aspects of our business not only creates an environment where we can all grow and thrive but also increases our potential to produce work that better represents—and resonates with—the world around us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;monks.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Monks is seeking an experienced client-facing&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Data Engineer (Marketing &amp;amp; BI) &lt;/strong&gt;to drive data and analytics delivery across marketing, audience, and e-commerce engagements for both small and large enterprise clients.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role that blends business and data responsibilities. Your time will be split approximately 70% on client delivery and 30% internal (capability building, reusable assets, innovation, growth, etc). You’ll be focused on SQL-based data modelling and analytics delivery, and you’ll run client workshops and stakeholder management, while also building out solutions in the broader BI space, executing technical implementations across a range of analytics and cloud data platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has a history of working with modern data products (e.g. BigQuery, Snowflake, Databricks, Redshift), and a proven track record of experience with the modern data stack based on cloud technologies, including data transformation, orchestration, warehousing and modelling, as well as BI and dashboard design using tools like Looker Studio, Power BI or Tableau.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Monks?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll help clients shape data pathways, translate data into insights and needs-based recommendations, deploy and configure the right tools, and improve data reliability, speed to insight, and KPI consistency. Working in the broader Data capability at Monks, this position offers opportunities for growth within our wider APAC data team with clear channels of progression into more senior roles, the ability to participate in innovation on projects and product development, and the potential to advance the practice of analytics and data from the forefront.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead requirements discovery and translate business questions into data/measurement solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design data models (dimensional/star schemas) to support scalable reporting and self-serve analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and model data across various cloud data warehouses (BigQuery/Snowflake/Databricks/Redshift) from marketing, web/app, and e-commerce sources; exact platform varies by client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Articulate, design and develop BI dashboards and custom reporting experiences using tools such as Looker Studio, Power BI and Tableau.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish data quality, monitoring, documentation, and governance practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with analytics/measurement teams on tracking approaches (GA4/GTM) to ensure usable downstream data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present insights and recommendations to senior stakeholders; influence roadmaps, estimation and prioritisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute reusable assets (templates, data patterns, dashboard standards) to the wider Monks APAC data capability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 4+ years experience in data engineering / analytics engineering / BI engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 year experience in client-facing delivery, consultancy or agency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with BigQuery and at least one other cloud data platform (Snowflake, Databricks, Redshift, etc) required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert SQL skills, primarily in an ETL/ELT context; we are BigQuery first, but some Python is also favoured.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong dimensional modeling (star schemas), warehouse design, and metric/KPI definition for analytics use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building BI dashboards (Looker Studio, Power BI, Tableau).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with mainstream analytics platforms and data collection approaches, including Google Marketing Platform tooling (GTM, GA4, etc) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with transformation and orchestration tools including dbt, Airflow, Dagster or Prefect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with broader enterprise BI platforms such as Looker (LookML/custom visualisations) or Datorama.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of the adtech/martech/data landscape; CRM &amp;amp; CDP familiarity is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Monks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks is the global, purely digital, unitary operating brand of S4Capital plc. With a legacy of innovation and specialized expertise, Monks combines an extraordinary range of global marketing and technology services to accelerate business possibilities and redefine how brands and businesses interact with the world. Its integration of systems and workflows delivers unfettered content production, scaled experiences, enterprise-grade technology and data science fueled by AI—managed by the industry’s best and most diverse digital talent—to help the world’s trailblazing companies outmaneuver and outpace their competition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services. It has remained a constant presence on Adweek’s Fastest Growing lists (2019-23), ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-23) and is the only partner to have been placed in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). In addition to being named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023), Monks has been recognized by Business Intelligence in its 2024 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Awards program in three categories: the Individual category, Organizational Winner in AI Strategic Planning and AI Product for its service Monks.Flow. Monks has also garnered the title of Webby Production Company of the Year (2021-24), won a record number of FWAs and has earned a spot on Newsweek’s Top 100 Global Most Loved Workplaces 2023.&lt;/p&gt;
