&lt;p&gt;Monks is looking for a Delivery Manager based in Colombia to own the DAM operations for one of our largest global clients. You’ll manage a high-volume, fast-paced system, enable global creative teams to find and deliver assets quickly, and act as the primary point of contact for DAM-related training, first-line support, licensing and compliance. You’ll collaborate closely with regional teams, in-house developers and external partners to keep the DAM, asset library and integrated workflows running smoothly and accurately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the DAM: ensure assets are uploaded, tagged with correct metadata, and organized so assets are discoverable in seconds. Keep folder structures clean and enforce naming/ingest standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-line support: respond to user questions from creative, ops, account teams and external agencies; triage issues and document resolutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training &amp;amp; documentation: develop and deliver training materials and onboarding for new and existing users on the DAM, review/approval platform and asset library.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;QA &amp;amp; governance: monitor asset integrity, usage rights and compliance; implement and enforce processes to reduce errors and drive consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration: build and maintain relationships with internal teams across your region (North &amp;amp; Latin America).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product feedback &amp;amp; issue tracking: log bugs, feature requests and workflow enhancements with internal development teams; close the loop on fixes and improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock &amp;amp; licensing management: liaise with stock houses globally; review, acquire and distribute stock assets and licenses; advise and enforce licensing and procurement policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder liaison: act as the bridge between creative, account, legal and procurement teams to resolve pricing, licensing and compliance questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years professional experience in Digital Asset Management within advertising, marketing or similar creative environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with a DAM system (Adobe AEM preferred); experience as an administrator, librarian/curator or DAM operator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of creative asset types and formats (image, video, audio, fonts, animation, templates, etc.) and how they’re used in production and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal English communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with creative, operations and account teams and comfortable training end users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solver with a process-driven mindset: able to document workflows, write training materials and translate user needs into clear feature requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and collaboratively across time zones; manage changing priorities and tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills — you’re a relationship builder who can navigate a global organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
