&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve mastered Illustrator, Indesign, Figma and Photoshop skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to keep your files, layers, and folders super-organized, even if you’re a creative mess outside of Photoshop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to work with dielines and different types of vendor specs for print projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Although you work under the supervision of a lead who guarantees the quality of the work, you must also have the ability to work independently if the project requires it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can contribute to different stages of the production process, from creating design libraries, image generating and sourcing, language versioning, resizing for other platforms, and preparing files for delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are enthusiastic about utilising AI as a tool to create efficiencies and possibilities outside of what is possible with manual work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are detail-oriented, pixel-perfect, methodic and solution-oriented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re always on the lookout for process efficiencies. Part of the responsibilities may include helping other designers with less experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can handle repetitive tasks and stay focused.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re well-versed in English and production tricks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a clear communicator and are happy to work with designers from all over the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
