&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Digital Asset Coordinator, &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;you’ll be the main point of contact for all traffic-related needs across TV and Digital Media. This role provides a huge opportunity to adjoin the technical and production worlds, managing asset lifecycles and ensuring flawless distribution for brave, innovative brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an organized and administrative specialist, you will be responsible for navigating network clearance and coordinating with media agencies and Ad Ops teams. The ideal candidate will be proactive, hands-on, result-oriented, and able to work under the pressure of tight deadlines and high accuracy. In other words, a self-starter with a strong work ethic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create AD-IDs for all assets and develop creative naming conventions for all digital video assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and obtain Network Clearance for creative assets through every stage of development, from Script to Rough Cut and Final.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately fill out and distribute traffic sheets for partner media agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and assist the Ad Ops team with CSDs (Campaign Specification Documents).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upload and traffic creative assets directly into distribution platforms like Tandem and Innovid.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process vendor invoices efficiently to ensure timely payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compile and send talent reports to the Talent Manager whenever required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate flexibility and willingness to take on administrative tasks in new areas of the industry as needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience you already have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2 years of professional experience as a Traffic Manager or in a similar role; &lt;strong&gt;agency experience is required&lt;/strong&gt;, preferably within the digital production industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with content, media production, and right clearance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and administrative skills with a keen eye for accuracy under tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm to work collaboratively within a team, but also the independence to work with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced english&lt;/strong&gt; with excellent written and verbal communication skills (any other language is a bonus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with CPG (Consumer Packaged Goods) Brands&lt;strong&gt; is considered a strong plus.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
