&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Information About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that this position requires working &lt;strong&gt;Wednesday through Sunday. Wednesday-Friday from 7:00 PM to 1:00 AM and Saturday / Sunday and holidays from 9 AM - 5PM.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Due to the nature of the role and the event calendar, candidates should be comfortable working on &lt;strong&gt;public holidays. &lt;/strong&gt;This role involves collaborating with &lt;strong&gt;cross-functional teams and stakeholders across multiple regions&lt;/strong&gt;, requiring strong communication, adaptability, and the ability to work effectively in a global environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While the role follows a fixed schedule, Monks offers flexibility when business priorities require attendance at events, meetings, or activations outside of regular working hours. In such cases, schedules can be adjusted accordingly to ensure a balanced workload.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and implement social media and communication campaigns to align with marketing strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on content calendars -along with the social strategist &amp;amp; the content creator- and make them come true, including the timely publishing of social media posts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide engaging text for social media responses and copies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to comments and customer queries in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with data analysts&amp;nbsp; and social strategists to provide monthly and quarterly reports and optimization opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct social listening to identify trends and insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with social strategy, account management and creatives to ensure social media channels are on brand at all times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up-to-date with digital technology trends and identify opportunities for growth and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze the conversation around the brand daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze brand performance (analytical skills essential) to drive effective results for client KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cover brand related events in real-time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background &amp;amp; Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 years of experience in Community Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of social media good practices in terms of formats and tone of voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify and track relevant community metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of metrics, social listening tools and digital reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-facing experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in developing or implementing community manager strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal communication skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writing skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the Emplifi tool is a plus but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
