&lt;p&gt;At its core, Media.Monks is designed to help brands navigate the &quot;always-on&quot; digital world through a philosophy of &lt;strong&gt;&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;unitary structure&lt;strong&gt;&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;—meaning no silos, no borders, and a relentless focus on speed, quality, and value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a global collection of talent—makers, thinkers, and tech-enthusiasts—working across 30+ countries. As a global company, we recognise the diversity of our workforce and the importance of promoting a culture of tolerance and acceptance. We are dedicated to establishing a positive and inclusive work environment and extends to all interactions within the company and its business activities worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Payments &amp;amp; Cash &amp;amp; Banking Specialist to work in our global Finance team. Based in &lt;strong&gt;Kuala Lumpur&lt;/strong&gt;, this role will perform payments, cash&amp;nbsp; and banking activities for entities across the region working to standardised processes, and working in an efficient, and compliant manner while meeting local operational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will report to the &lt;strong&gt;Regional P2P Lead &lt;/strong&gt;and will work within the P2P team to ensure the timely processing of invoices and other payable transactions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being supplier- and customer-focused, this role will partner with both to ensure invoices are paid on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on the NetSuite OneWorld ERP to ensure timely execution of payments to suppliers and employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the execution of scheduled payment runs from start to finish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with invoice processing team to ensure accurate generation of payment proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validating and managing requests for urgent payment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily cash operations including monitoring cash positions, processing bank transactions, and reconciling accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile bank statements and resolve discrepancies in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records of all cash and banking activities for reporting and audit purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support month-end and year-end closing processes by preparing cash and banking reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in implementing and maintaining cash management tools within Netsuite OneWorld to optimize cash flow and banking operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with corporate treasury policies, accounting standards, and local regulations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting or a similar field preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of ERP systems’ functionality, specifically NetSuite, is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2 years’ experience working within a Payments and/or Cash &amp;amp; Banking function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to monitor complex data workflows and identify issues before they impact the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and&amp;nbsp;command of written and spoken English&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deliver accurate results under tight deadlines and manage competing priorities effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
