&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be a senior creative force on high-profile brand marketing campaigns spanning social content, hero video, motion graphics, and typographic animation. Operating within a dedicated client team, you&#39;ll own the animation process end-to-end — from concept and pre-production through final delivery — collaborating with creative directors, producers, illustrators, and animators across a global team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At this level, nobody oversees your craft — you set the bar. You&#39;re expected to drive quality and efficiency, mentor junior and semi-senior animators, push new techniques and tools, and serve as an internal ambassador for generative AI in the animation workflow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full animation lifecycle — pre-production assessment, creative scoping, execution, and final delivery — across social assets, complex hero videos, and multi-platform campaign toolkits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead early-stage creative ideation alongside art directors and creative leads, translating briefs and copy into high-quality motion work across formats, languages, and dimensions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimize production templates that improve speed and consistency for the broader global animation team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain brand integrity across all deliverables — consistent across ad formats, platforms, and languages — while proactively flagging risks and unfeasible timelines before they become problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion and integrate generative AI tools into your workflow, staying ahead of market trends and helping the team adopt new techniques and software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present work and contribute to creative conversations with support from the craft director; collaborate with producers and cross-functional teams across multiple offices worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and mentor junior and semi-senior animators, actively sharing progress, problems, and creative solutions across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in motion design and 2D animation, with a portfolio demonstrating ownership across brand campaigns, social content, and hero video production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in After Effects, Premiere, Photoshop, Illustrator, and Figma — you know how to do the basics right, and when to break the rules for creative effect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with generative AI tools — Runway, MidJourney, Adobe Firefly, Whisk, or similar — with a genuine drive to stay current as the toolset evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong visual design sensibility across typography, colour, layout, and composition in both static and motion contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage your own time, flag risks early, and deliver high-quality work under tight deadlines — independently, without hand-holding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate to advanced English proficiency (written and verbal) — enough to work fluidly with international teams, communicate blockers clearly, and present creative work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset — equally comfortable leading a creative direction, mentoring a junior, or taking notes from a craft director.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2D character animation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3D animation (C4D / Blender)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Storyboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lottie / Rive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency / production background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social platform specs (Meta, TikTok, YT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;#LI-MS1 &lt;/span&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Monks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks is the global, digital-first, data-driven, unitary operating brand of S4 Capital plc. With a legacy of innovation and specialized expertise, Monks combines an extraordinary range of global Marketing and Technology Services to redefine how brands interact with the world. Through Monks.Flow, its flagship AI ecosystem for marketing orchestration, Monks transforms marketing into a growth engine, collapsing timelines and connecting brands to culture in real time. By deploying bespoke intelligent agents across disciplines and delivering culturally relevant, high-impact creative and digital solutions, Monks solves key critical business challenges across the entire brand enterprise to help brands sustain long-term impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services, ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-25) and remains the only partner featured in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). Named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023) and The One Show’s inaugural AI Pioneer Organization, Monks was also awarded Business Intelligence Group’s 2025 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Award in both the Organizational and AI Product categories. As a trusted partner to cutting-edge innovators in tech, Monks earned titles such as Optimizely Experimentation Partner of the Year (2025), runner-up for the Adobe Firefly Partner Award (2024), and Workato’s AI Visionary Customer Impact Award (2024). Additionally, Monks achieved a record-breaking number of FWAs and continues to hold the most of any partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a respectful and empowering work environment for all people to freely express themselves amongst colleagues who embrace diversity in all respects. Including fresh voices and unique points of view in all aspects of our business not only creates an environment where we can all grow and thrive but also increases our potential to produce work that better represents—and resonates with—the world around us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;monks.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Art Director, you’ll lead the development of social first ideas and campaigns alongside other creatives — shaping social campaigns from initial concept through execution. You’ll craft compelling creative visions, present your thinking to clients, be hands on and provide art direction to designers and production teams, all while becoming a true brand expert and upholding a consistently high creative bar. We are looking for someone who is passionate about seeking new opportunities to create impactful, innovative work — a conceptual thinker and go-getter who thrives in a fast-paced environment, brings a strong point of view, and stays humble while championing bold creative ideas. You’ll help us maintain an environment that encourages expression, inclusivity, and collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;This role is in Culver City, CA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt; (8559 Higiera St., Culver City, CA); hybrid role!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of original, conceptual social ideas that align with brand strategy and client goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate ideas and designs to senior members of the creative team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Sr. Copywriter and Content Creator to bring campaigns from concept to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate briefs into compelling storytelling and visual narratives across social, digital, and emerging formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Producers to plan photo/video shoots and manage production needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate proactively with team leads on timelines, blockers, and deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, both verbal and listening abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain consistent creative quality and become a brand expert&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a standard-bearer for our company culture and values&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work within brand style guides to produce work that is both original and on-brand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain design systems, templates, and asset libraries for efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with both B2B and B2C marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Animation experience, and comfort working with and directing a motion designer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert in (Adobe Creative Suite, Figma, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in Los Angeles, CA, metro area&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The essentials:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong conceptual portfolio demonstrating social media ideas, not just execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8+ years of conceptual art direction experience (in house or agency experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step in to concept, write up, and execute ideas when additional support is needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert experience in social media content and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt quickly to shifting priorities and time-sensitive requests with multiple iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to accept and receive constructive design feedback from senior members of the creative team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not a must, but a plus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual (English / Spanish)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Animation skills (AfterEffects)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
