&lt;p&gt;At Monks, Senior Designers are the backbone of creative execution at scale. You bring equal parts craft, systems thinking, and creative ambition — translating brand vision into high-quality assets that perform across global campaigns, platforms, and moments. This is not just a production role. You&#39;ll operate confidently in the space between established brand guidelines and new creative territory, pushing boundaries while ensuring every deliverable meets the highest standard of quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work at speed and at scale — owning asset delivery for high-velocity programs and setting the craft bar for the work that goes out the door.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of high-volume, high-quality creative assets across global campaigns, maintaining brand consistency at every touchpoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion brand integrity across regions — ensuring visual systems, style guides, and design standards are applied with precision and intent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate confidently in the &quot;gray space&quot; — blending established brand guidelines with fresh creative thinking to find new ways of expressing the brand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and evolve style guides and design systems built for scale, ensuring assets are consistent, adaptable, and platform-ready&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own quality assurance across deliverables — serving as the final reviewer before work reaches senior stakeholder or client review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide and supervise a team of production designers, providing clear creative direction, feedback, and support to ensure efficient, on-brand output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push the boundaries of what&#39;s possible within Figma — leveraging its full capabilities to create outstanding designs and invent smarter ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with creative directors, strategists, producers, and technologists to deliver solutions that are both creatively strong and commercially effective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present and articulate design decisions clearly and confidently to internal teams and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of design trends, cultural moments, and emerging tools — bringing fresh references and creative energy to every project&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a Designer or Art Director in an agency or fast-paced creative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio demonstrating exceptional craft, range, and the ability to work across brand, campaign, and digital experiences at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working on global campaigns with a deep understanding of design consistency, brand systems, and regional adaptation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level proficiency in Figma — including design systems, component libraries, and collaborative workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in style guide development, asset production, and quality assurance across high-volume deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or supervising production designers, with the ability to give clear, constructive creative direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker who can design for scale without sacrificing craft or creative intent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with AI-powered design tools and emerging workflows that accelerate creative production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on large-scale retail, tech, or e-commerce enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motion design skills and experience with animation or video asset production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with design for performance — understanding how creative decisions impact campaign effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
