&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a &lt;em&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/em&gt;, you’ll lead cross-functional teams to define product strategy, identify market and user opportunities, and deliver innovative digital products that meet customer needs and support business goals. You’ll serve as a trusted advisor to clients, guide products through the full lifecycle, and help shape a strong product culture focused on continuous improvement, agility, and measurable impact.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve&lt;/strong&gt; as a trusted advisor to client stakeholders, providing strategic guidance and acting as the primary point of contact for product-related decisions, updates, and inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conduct&lt;/strong&gt; market, competitive, business, and user research to identify opportunities and translate insights into actionable product strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define&lt;/strong&gt; and articulate long-term product vision, strategy, and roadmaps aligned with business goals, market trends, customer feedback, and end-user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate&lt;/strong&gt; with Engineering, Design, Delivery, and other key stakeholders to ensure successful product development, launch, adoption, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Oversee&lt;/strong&gt; the end-to-end product lifecycle from ideation through launch and beyond, including requirements definition, feature prioritization, and trade-off management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish&lt;/strong&gt; KPIs and success metrics to measure product performance, analyze results, and drive ongoing product improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify&lt;/strong&gt; product delivery risks and challenges, developing mitigation strategies and contingency plans to support successful outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion&lt;/strong&gt; agile methodologies, experimentation, feedback loops, and continuous improvement across product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay&lt;/strong&gt; current on industry trends, emerging technologies, and product management best practices, sharing insights to spark innovation and elevate team performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor&lt;/strong&gt; associate and mid-level Product Managers, providing feedback, guidance, and support for their professional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve&lt;/strong&gt; product management processes, tools, and methodologies to enhance team efficiency, collaboration, and consistency across initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Promote&lt;/strong&gt; a strong product culture centered on customer-centricity, agility, experimentation, knowledge sharing, and continuous learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+&lt;/strong&gt; years of professional experience in technology projects related to digital products, software design, and/or software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record managing the end-to-end software product lifecycle for a product or suite of products with multiple features, complex requirements, diverse stakeholder needs, and a dedicated team&lt;/li&gt;
