&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a highly analytical &lt;strong&gt;Senior Specialist, FP&amp;amp;A&lt;/strong&gt; who thrives at the intersection of Corporate Finance, Strategic Analysis, and Data Engineering. In this role, you will report numbers and will be the strategic voice that interprets them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bridge the gap between complex financial processes and executive decision-making. Your mission is to maintain a robust global financial data pipeline while providing deep-dive analyses that help stakeholders understand the &quot;why&quot; behind the results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the month-end closing analysis, providing clear commentary on variances (Actuals vs. Budget/Forecast). You will transform raw data into executive-level reports that highlight trends, risks, and opportunities for the NAMER and Global regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a key finance partner for Regional Directors and Department Heads. You will translate complex technical logic and financial data into actionable insights, helping non-finance leaders manage their budgets and headcount effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P&amp;amp;L Architecture &amp;amp; Profitability:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and optimize multi-dimensional P&amp;amp;L reporting. You will analyze profitability down to the Client and Departmental level, ensuring that global allocations and intercompany markups are both accurate and strategically aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Integration &amp;amp; Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain API connections (Workday, Salesforce, Greenhouse) to automate data flow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Ingestion &amp;amp; SQL Modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect complex SQL queries within BigQuery to consolidate global data. You will ensure that the &quot;Actuals vs. Forecast&quot; reconciliations are seamless and require minimal manual intervention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Integrity &amp;amp; Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the final gatekeeper for data accuracy. You will identify logic errors or &quot;noise&quot; in financial models before they reach executive reviews, ensuring 100% confidence in the numbers presented to the CFO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Professional Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance Foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced understanding of P&amp;amp;L structures, Budgeting/Forecasting cycles, and the nuances between Management and Statutory reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Engineering &amp;amp; Scripting:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;SQL (BigQuery)&lt;/strong&gt; is essential. Experience with &lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;Javascript/Apps Script&lt;/strong&gt; for API handling and workflow automation is highly valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BI &amp;amp; Visualization:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of designing executive dashboards in &lt;strong&gt;Looker Studio&lt;/strong&gt; (or similar) that drive strategic decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with ERPs (&lt;strong&gt;Netsuite/Lucanet&lt;/strong&gt;) and CRM/HRIS tools (&lt;strong&gt;Salesforce, Workday, Greenhouse&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced English.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
