&lt;p&gt;You will play a key role in ensuring that art content and features are seamlessly integrated into the engine while maintaining the project’s artistic vision and respecting technical constraints.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role &amp;amp; Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with generalist to create 3D art and bring it into the engine&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support artists in using the 3D art pipeline and user-facing engine tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with artists to create high-quality 3D assets with a strong emphasis on materials, shaders, and surface realism&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review creative workflows and identify opportunities for tool and pipeline improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Unreal Engine art pipeline tools and extensions with a focus on usability and efficiency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve complex technical issues within the Unreal Engine asset pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with artists and QA to diagnose and fix production challenges&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure documentation is accessible and up to date for artists and technical teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help inspire and empower the art team to optimize their workflows and processes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in Unreal Engine Blueprints&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in Unreal Engine materials and shader development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of material graphs, PBR workflows, and real-time rendering principles ● Experience developing tools within Unreal Engine&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building configurators, automation tools, or similar systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of lighting, reflections, and surface response&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong teamwork and communication abilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively under deadlines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English (written and spoken); German is a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quick learner with a willingness to share knowledge&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with strong attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Naturally curious and proactive mindset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming knowledge (C++ and/or Python)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with USD (Universal Scene Description)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of automotive shading standards (e.g., car paint, clear coat, interiors) ● Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with premium brands or high-end productions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in additional 3D software (e.g., Maya, Blender)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automotive industry experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong time management skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of shading and materials&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of rendering pipelines (real-time and offline)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
