&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineering Team Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to join our growing team and drive the deployment and evolution of our MarTech platform and solutions. This is a hands-on leadership role—ideal for someone who still loves to ship code but is equally passionate about tackling client challenges, shaping technical direction, and collaborating cross-functionally. As a Team Lead, you’ll lead the engineering group of a cross-functional team composed of software engineers, a product manager, and UX/design. Our product is used by marketing teams in regulated industries across the world. You will serve as a Technical Subject Matter Expert (SME), partnering with the core client team and our platform team on long-term architecture, collaborating with Product Managers on roadmap planning, and working with other Team Leads across the organization to ensure cohesion and scalability in everything we build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a Technical Subject Matter Expert for our product, owning the technical direction and quality of solutions designed and deployed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement and innovation, including extended integrations with client technology and data systems beyond the immediate project scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the ongoing reliability and effectiveness of our product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to our MarTech platform&#39;s priorities and roadmap, working with our internal engineering team on technical architecture and long-term planning so they are always aligned with the needs and vision for our client engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers on the team to support their professional growth and technical development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive good engineering practices and processes, such as blameless post-mortems and automated testing, to ensure software stability and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The essentials:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience, ideally across the full stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of people management experience (Tech Lead, Engineering Manager, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing secure, scalable systems end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with TypeScript, Next.js, Node.js, and React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a hybrid technical/data role, bridging engineering and data-driven decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of secure integrations, API authentication, and OAuth 2.0 flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with domain-driven design or clean architecture patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI coding tools (Claude Code, Codex) to build software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not a must, but a plus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working in high-compliance environments (HIPAA, SOC2, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Terraform or other infrastructure as code tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience bootstrapping teams or greenfield systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
