&lt;p&gt;Remote (USA) &lt;em&gt;Note: Must be a U.S. citizen or a green card holder residing in the US.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an OS 2200 Applications Support Specialist to join our team, providing critical support for a major manufacturing client&#39;s core business applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers an opportunity to work with time-tested enterprise systems and contribute to ongoing modernization efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help a team of specialists provide on-call response and support for the client&#39;s Unisys 2200 application environment.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’ve got a flexible rotation schedule to ensure coverage while keeping our team happy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow and execute against customer-defined policies for incident escalation, change control, testing, and promotion into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform monitoring of mainframe databases to ensure data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and assess incidents, distinguishing between systems software issues and application anomalies or defects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement approved corrections and coordinate with change control procedures for timely remedy installation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the ongoing documentation and expansion of the knowledge base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise management on technical trends and potential impacts on the application environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone with (minimum) 3+ years of experience in managing, servicing, and supporting OS 2200 applications in an enterprise environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Must haves&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Unisys 2200 applications development and operations. Familiarity with OS 2200 systems support principles is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the DMS-1100 database system and TIP transaction processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of OS 2200 development tools, operational utilities, networking, and cross-platform integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the primary application technologies: COBOL and related development utilities. Experience with MASM (assembler) highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of job control using Executive Control Language (ECL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive under pressure to help remedy time-sensitive mission-critical issues&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great written and verbal communication skills, adapting comms as needed depending on the audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with data access methods, including DMS-1100, ISAM, and flat files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nice-to-haves&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with utilities related to development and operations: (SSG, CTS, DDP, FTP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to troubleshoot integration points with diverse external systems, such as VAX Shop Floor, Oracle ERP, Unix, Web/Java, and Windows platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
